<title>PHILIPPINES: Manila says buys 2.24 bln pesos sugar.</title>
<headline>Manila says buys 2.24 bln pesos sugar.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1997-04-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Philippines' National Food Authority said on Saturday it has so far bought 3.7 million 50 kg bags of raw sugar worth 2.24 billion pesos from local farmers since February 27.</p>
<p>The state agency was buying raw sugar at 610 pesos a bag to bid up domestic prices which were at a low 570 pesos before the buying programme started.</p>
<p>--MANILA NEWSROOM (63 2) 841-8936, FAX 817-6267</p>
